    <section class="detail-section" id="who" aria-labelledby="who-title">
      <div class="wrap detail-grid">
        <h2 id="who-title">Who is Ilmoo for?</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Ilmoo is a written internal whistleblowing channel under EU Directive 2019/1937 and Finland’s Whistleblower Protection Act 1171/2022. It is designed especially for Finnish organisations regularly employing at least 50 people.</p>
          <p>The obligation to establish a channel depends on the scope of the law. Special statutory rules can also cover smaller organisations, so headcount alone does not determine an organisation’s obligations.</p>
          <p class="note">Not sure? <a href="https://ilmoo.fi/self-check">Take the two-question self-check on ilmoo.fi <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
          <p>Each company gets its own subdomain, such as <span class="mono">yourcompany.ilmoo.fi</span>. Share the link on your website, intranet, onboarding materials and supplier portal so employees and other reporters can find the company’s channel.</p>
          <ul class="who-list">
            <li><b>Reporters</b>Employees and other reporters submit reports at the company’s own address without an account.</li>
            <li><b>Handlers</b>Acknowledge, investigate and reply to the reporter in one place.</li>
            <li><b>Administrators</b>Manage users, roles and channel settings.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="detail-section" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
      <div class="wrap detail-grid">
        <h2 id="how-title">How a report moves forward</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <ol class="timeline" aria-label="Report stages">
            <li><span class="t-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3>1. Report without an account</h3><p>The reporter submits a written report through the company’s channel without registering. Reports are anonymous by default and can include attachments.</p></li>
            <li><span class="t-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3>2. Return with a personal code</h3><p>The reporter receives a personal access code. They can keep using the same code to check the case status, read replies and exchange further messages with the handler.</p></li>
            <li><span class="t-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3>3. Investigate and respond</h3><p>The organisation’s handlers acknowledge the report, investigate and reply to the reporter. Attachments, internal notes and an audit trail keep a record of the handling process.</p></li>
          </ol>
          <h3>Keep statutory deadlines in view</h3>
          <p>Receipt is acknowledged within seven days of receiving a report. Feedback on action taken or planned is provided within three months of that acknowledgement. If no acknowledgement is sent, the three-month period starts when the seven-day period following receipt ends.</p>
          <p>The feedback deadline does not mean every investigation must be complete by then. The organisation’s handlers remain responsible for follow-up and meeting the deadlines.</p>
          <p>Email scatters reports across personal inboxes and blurs responsibilities. In Ilmoo, the report, the messages and the handling stay in one place. <a href="{{url:guide-wb}}">Read the whistleblowing channel guide</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="detail-section" id="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
      <div class="wrap detail-grid">
        <h2 id="features-title">Features</h2>
        <div>
          <div class="feature-groups">
            <section aria-labelledby="f1">
              <h3 id="f1">For reporters</h3>
              <ul class="ticks">
                <li>No reporter account needed; anonymous by default</li>
                <li>Attachments</li>
                <li>A personal access code for follow-up and messaging</li>
                <li>Available in Finnish, English and Swedish</li>
              </ul>
            </section>
            <section aria-labelledby="f2">
              <h3 id="f2">Staff permissions and tools</h3>
              <ul class="ticks">
                <li>Admin, handler and readonly roles for administration, case handling and viewing</li>
                <li>Email alerts to support case handling</li>
                <li>Admin statistics to monitor activity</li>
                <li>PDF and CSV exports for further use of the records</li>
                <li>Internal notes, attachments and an audit trail</li>
              </ul>
            </section>
            <section aria-labelledby="f3">
              <h3 id="f3">For the organisation</h3>
              <ul class="ticks">
                <li>A company subdomain, such as <span class="mono">yourcompany.ilmoo.fi</span></li>
                <li>Unlimited users with no per-seat add-ons</li>
                <li>All data stays in the EU</li>
                <li>Optionally, general feedback through the same channel, without statutory deadlines (ilmoo.fi)</li>
              </ul>
            </section>
            <section aria-labelledby="f4">
              <h3 id="f4">Written reports and audio recordings</h3>
              <p>Ilmoo’s core is written reporting and messaging. Reporters can also upload an audio recording as a report.</p>
              <p>A company can publish its own live phone number and instructions for arranging a meeting alongside the channel link. Ilmoo does not include a live telephone service: the company organises calls and meetings through its own process.</p>
            </section>
          </div>
          <div class="limits" id="limits">
            <h3>What Ilmoo doesn’t do</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Ilmoo does not include a live telephone service: the company organises calls and meetings through its own process.</li>
              <li>Responsibility doesn’t move to the service. The organisation’s handlers remain responsible for follow-up and meeting the deadlines.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="detail-section" id="privacy" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
      <div class="wrap detail-grid">
        <h2 id="privacy-title">Data protection and responsibilities</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Ilmoo is developed by AI Generation Oy. The customer organisation is the controller of report data, and the Ilmoo service provider acts as the processor.</p>
          <p>Content is encrypted at rest, and access codes are stored as hashes. The service includes legal pages and data processing agreement (DPA) templates under Article 28 of the GDPR.</p>
          <p class="note">According to ilmoo.fi, reports are encrypted at rest with AES-256-GCM, end-to-end encryption is optional, and no IP address is stored for anonymous reports. <a href="https://ilmoo.fi/legal/subprocessors">Service providers and data transfers on ilmoo.fi <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
          <p class="source">Legal framework: <a href="https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2019/1937/oj">Directive (EU) 2019/1937</a> and <a href="https://www.finlex.fi/fi/lainsaadanto/2022/1171">Finland’s Act 1171/2022 (in Finnish)</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

